  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Microservices have a larger attack surface than monoliths. Each service is a potential entry point. Security must be layered."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Key Concepts"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "key-terms",
      "data": {
        "terms": [
          {
            "term": "Attack Surface",
            "definition": "The total number of points where an attacker can enter."
          },
          {
            "term": "Defense in Depth",
            "definition": "Layering multiple security controls."
          },
          {
            "term": "Authentication",
            "definition": "Verifying identity."
          },
          {
            "term": "Authorization",
            "definition": "Verifying permissions."
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Security Challenges"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "Large attack surface (many services)",
          "Network communication (interception risk)",
          "Distributed authentication",
          "Secret management across services",
          "Compliance across services"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Defense in Depth"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Layer security controls: network security, service authentication, authorization, encryption, auditing. No single control is sufficient."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Security Layers"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "data": {
        "headers": ["Layer", "Controls"],
        "rows": [
          ["Network", "Firewalls, TLS, network policies"],
          ["Service", "Authentication, authorization"],
          ["Data", "Encryption at rest and in transit"],
          ["Application", "Input validation, rate limiting"],
          ["Audit", "Logging, monitoring"]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Principles"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "Least privilege: grant minimum permissions",
          "Zero trust: never trust, always verify",
          "Separation of duties",
          "Fail secure: deny by default"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Architecture"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "mermaid",
      "data": {
